### API smoke collection — Crypto Portfolio server
###
### Task: P0-01. Companion to docs/BASELINE.md.
### Run with the REST Client extension (VS Code) or `httpyac`/`kulala`.
###
### Start the server first:
###   npm start --prefix server
###
### Note: server/index.js loads only the root .env, which has no MONGO_URI,
### so the server runs on the JSON fallback path. See docs/BASELINE.md.

@host = http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}
@addr = 0xcb9d0aa389456eb5a46c772f38b59c40b092ebcc
@badAddr = 0xzzz
@unknownAddr = 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000001

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. Health
### DB down  -> 503 { success:false, status:"degraded", db:"disconnected" }
### DB up    -> 200 { success:true,  status:"ok",       db:"connected"    }
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/health

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. Market — coin list
### Upstream up   -> 200 { success:true, count:3, data:[…] }
### Upstream down -> 500 { success:false, message:"CoinGecko API error: …" }
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/api/market/coins?limit=3

### 2b. Same call again — exercises the cache-hit path (P1-01 / P1-02).
GET {{host}}/api/market/coins?limit=3

### 2c. Non-numeric limit — falls back to the default of 100, does not 400.
GET {{host}}/api/market/coins?limit=abc

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. Market — coin details (no cache, direct CoinGecko proxy)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/api/market/coins/bitcoin

### 3b. Unknown coin -> 404 { success:false, message:"Coin not found: …" }
GET {{host}}/api/market/coins/definitely-not-a-coin

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. Transactions — count
### -> 200 { success:true, count:<n> }
### Declared before /:address; reordering breaks this route.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/api/transactions/count

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. Transactions — by address
### -> 200 { success:true, data:[…], pagination:{ total,page,limit,totalPages,hasNextPage } }
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/api/transactions/{{addr}}?page=1&limit=5

### 5b. Malformed address -> 200 with an empty array. No validation today (P3-03).
GET {{host}}/api/transactions/{{badAddr}}

### 5c. Page past the end -> 200, empty data, echoes the requested page.
GET {{host}}/api/transactions/{{addr}}?page=99

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 6. Watchlist — read
### -> 200. Unknown wallet is 200 with coins:[], NOT 404.
### In fallback mode every addedAt is stamped at read time — do not diff it.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/api/watchlist/{{addr}}

### 6b. Unknown wallet -> 200 { data: { walletAddress, coins: [] } }
GET {{host}}/api/watchlist/{{unknownAddr}}

### 6c. Malformed address -> 200. No validation today (P1-09).
GET {{host}}/api/watchlist/{{badAddr}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 7. Watchlist — add
### -> 200, echoes the full post-write list. Re-adding is a silent no-op.
### Pair this with request 8 so server/data/watchlist.json ends unchanged.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{host}}/api/watchlist/{{addr}}/coins
Content-Type: application/json

{ "coinId": "solana" }

### 7b. Missing coinId -> 400 { success:false, message:"coinId is required in the request body." }
POST {{host}}/api/watchlist/{{addr}}/coins
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 8. Watchlist — remove (undoes request 7)
### -> 200, echoes the post-delete list.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
DELETE {{host}}/api/watchlist/{{addr}}/coins/solana

### 8b. Unknown wallet -> 404. Asymmetric with GET, which returns 200.
DELETE {{host}}/api/watchlist/{{unknownAddr}}/coins/solana

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 9. Unmatched routes -> 404 { success:false, message:"Route not found." }
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/api/nope

### 9b. Root is a 404 — Express serves no static files.
GET {{host}}/

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 10. CORS — currently CORS_ORIGIN=* so this is echoed back (P1-14).
### After P1-14 this must return no Access-Control-Allow-Origin header.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/api/market/coins?limit=1
Origin: https://evil.example
